## Why This Is Asked
Tests for data export reflect real user needs and often fail on data mismatch or flaky downloads. This question probes data seeding, UI actions, file verification, and cross-browser handling.

## Key Concepts
- Data seeding and isolation
- End-to-end file download verification
- Network/mocked API endpoints
- Cross-browser testing strategies

## Code Example
```javascript
// Playwright example snippet
test('export selected rows', async ({ page, browserName }) => {
  await page.goto('/dashboard');
  await seedData(20);
  await page.click('#filter');
  await page.check('input[name="select-row-1"]');
  await page.check('input[name="select-row-2"]');
  const [ download ] = await Promise.all([
    page.waitForEvent('download'),
    page.click('#export-csv')
  ]);
  const path = await download.path();
  // read and verify CSV content deterministically
  const csv = await require('fs').promises.readFile(path, 'utf8');
  // parse and validate headers + 2 selected rows by IDs
});
```

